    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and it meets all four requirements. `pytest -q` passes (1 test), and a separate check against a stub transport confirmed the behaviour.\n\n**How it works:**\n- It builds the SDK's `DefaultHttpxClient` with `timeout=httpx.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)`, which gives connect 5 seconds and read, write and pool 30 seconds. This keeps the SDK's default connection limits and redirect handling.\n- A `\"request\"` event hook on that client logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The SDK sends each retry through the same client, so retries are logged too.\n- It passes `transport` straight to the HTTP client, so the tests' stub is used. When it's `None`, httpx uses its normal transport.\n- It returns `OpenAI(api_key=..., timeout=..., max_retries=2, http_client=...)`. I also set the timeout on the `OpenAI` object itself because the SDK sends its own timeout with every request, which overrides whatever is set on the HTTP client.\n\n**Check:** I used a stub transport that fails the first request with a 500 and then succeeds, and ran `rewrite_query` through it. The log showed `POST https://api.openai.com/v1/responses` twice, once for the first attempt and once for the retry. The timeouts were `connect=5.0, read=30.0, write=30.0, pool=30.0` on both the `OpenAI` object and the HTTP client, and `max_retries` was 2.\n\nI couldn't use Context7 because its monthly quota is used up, so I read the installed `openai==2.44.0` source instead. I didn't change any dependencies.\n\nThe check script `_check.py` is still in the project root because deleting it needed permission that wasn't granted. Please delete it (`rm _check.py`)."
  },
